#!/bin/bash
# Fresh-state check, step 2 (plan phase 4): records whether the Cáptalo
# defaults domain exists; if it does, exports it to .local/shell/, flushes
# and verifies the copy by re-reading it, and only then deletes the domain.
# Touches only com.thecreativetoken.captalo. Quit Cáptalo first.
set -eu
# CAPTALO_DEFAULTS_DOMAIN and CAPTALO_DEFAULTS_DIR exist only for the script tests.
DOMAIN=${CAPTALO_DEFAULTS_DOMAIN:-com.thecreativetoken.captalo}
ROOT=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
DIR=${CAPTALO_DEFAULTS_DIR:-"$ROOT/.local/shell"}
STAMP=$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)
mkdir -p "$DIR"
if pgrep -fx /Applications/Captalo.app/Contents/MacOS/Captalo >/dev/null; then
  echo "defaults-backup: Cáptalo is running; quit it first (make install records its PID)." >&2
  exit 1
fi
# A deleted domain can still read back as an empty dictionary: empty means absent.
is_empty() { [ "$(defaults export "$DOMAIN" - 2>/dev/null | plutil -convert json -o - - 2>/dev/null)" = "{}" ] || ! defaults read "$DOMAIN" >/dev/null 2>&1; }
xml() { plutil -convert xml1 -o - "$1"; }
if is_empty; then
  echo "absent" > "$DIR/defaults-$STAMP.state"
  echo "defaults-backup: domain absent; recorded $DIR/defaults-$STAMP.state"
  exit 0
fi
BACKUP="$DIR/defaults-$STAMP.plist"
defaults export "$DOMAIN" "$BACKUP"
sync
plutil -lint "$BACKUP" >/dev/null
LIVE=$(mktemp -t captalo-defaults)
defaults export "$DOMAIN" "$LIVE"
if ! xml "$LIVE" | cmp -s - <(xml "$BACKUP"); then
  rm -f "$LIVE"
  echo "defaults-backup: verification failed; domain kept" >&2
  exit 1
fi
rm -f "$LIVE"
echo "present" > "$DIR/defaults-$STAMP.state"
defaults delete "$DOMAIN"
echo "defaults-backup: exported to $BACKUP and deleted the domain"
